<title>USA: Inland to sell stake in Wabush Iron Ore.</title>
<headline>Inland to sell stake in Wabush Iron Ore.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inland Steel Co said Thursday it reached an agreement to sell its 15 percent interest in the Wabush IronOre mine to the managing partner, Cleveland-Cliffs Inc.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The transaction, pending required approvals, is expected to close later this month or in the second quarter.</p>
<p>&quot;This action is another step in our efforts to lower fixed costs and maintain the proper balance between our iron ore supplies and needs,&quot; said Inland president Dale Wiersbe in a statement.</p>
<p>		((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
